From 274171fbc86cb3235e14fa4dfbfe9c6b518427f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:11:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: piano_mca: add the factory fast-charge
 path

The factory charges at 12.4 A in four stages with a 4550 mV cell target only
when an authenticated adapter and both authenticated cell gauges agree, the
cells are inside the factory temperature window and below the tail-charge
state of charge. Otherwise the same hardware keeps the ordinary path.

Add that policy: the two FFC temperature rows with their stage currents and
tail termination, the cycle and state-of-health voltage derating from the
active BAA configuration, the buck charger's cutoff above 4480 mV, the
sharing budget for the PMIC stage, and the factory weighted board
temperature as a standard thermal zone.

Gauge mode changes only with the pump stopped; a raised PMIC float voltage
must not outlive the mode that asked for it, so a lost pause is retried from
the poll.
